{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide takes you from a wired Swidux app to a fully gated feature with paywall presentation, entitlement observation, restore, and manage-subscription support. It covers state and action wiring, implementing a "},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", presenting the sheet, gating a feature, and previewing in pro state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For an API-level reference of every type and action, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". For where domain plugins fit in the dispatch cycle, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Before you start","anchor":"Before-you-start","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide assumes:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You have a Swidux app already wired up — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppReducer"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore"},{"type":"text","text":" exist and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If you’re not there yet, follow "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" first."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You have a purchase backend in mind. RevenueCat is the path of least resistance, but vanilla StoreKit or a custom server work just as well — the plugin doesn’t care."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","level":2,"anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product to your app target in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPaywall\",","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Step 2: Add state and actions","level":2,"anchor":"Step-2-Add-state-and-actions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a paywall slice to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@SwiduxNested","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a paywall case to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ AppState.swift","import SwiduxPaywall","","@SwiduxState","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @SwiduxNested var paywall: PaywallState = .init()","    \/\/ … other slices","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"code":["\/\/ AppAction.swift","import SwiduxPaywall","","enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case paywall(PaywallAction)","    \/\/ … other cases","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin owns reducing for ","type":"text"},{"code":".paywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" actions, so the root reducer should fall through:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ AppReducer.swift","case .paywall:","    return nil"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Step 3: Provide a `PaywallService`","level":2,"anchor":"Step-3-Provide-a-PaywallService"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin needs a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer that talks to your purchase backend. Pick the path that matches your backend.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Path A: RevenueCat (recommended)","level":3,"anchor":"Path-A-RevenueCat-recommended"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" companion package and use the supplied "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":". No bridging code on your side."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\", from: \"1.0.0\"),"]},{"code":["import SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","","let service = RevenueCatPaywallService()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The companion package also ships "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI"},{"type":"text","text":", a SwiftUI sheet built on RevenueCatUI that hands purchase results back through the plugin. See its README for configuration (API key, entitlement identifiers)."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Path B: StoreKit or custom backend","level":3,"anchor":"Path-B-StoreKit-or-custom-backend"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For any non-RevenueCat backend, implement "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. The protocol is small:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPaywall","","struct MyPaywallService: PaywallService {","    func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot {","        \/\/ Fetch the current entitlement once.","        return EntitlementSnapshot()","    }","","    func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot> {","        AsyncStream { continuation in","            \/\/ Yield a new snapshot each time the entitlement changes.","            \/\/ Call continuation.finish() when the source ends.","        }","    }","","    func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot {","        \/\/ Run a restore against the user's account and return the result.","        return EntitlementSnapshot()","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A vanilla StoreKit conformer iterates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transaction.currentEntitlements"},{"type":"text","text":" and listens to "},{"code":"Transaction.updates","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a custom server conformer hits whatever endpoint reports the user’s entitlement.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Previews and tests","type":"heading","anchor":"Previews-and-tests"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the built-in "},{"code":"MockPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for backend-agnostic previews:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let service = MockPaywallService(isPro: true)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’re on Path A, ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" also ships ","type":"text"},{"code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for RevenueCat-flavored previews.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Step 4: Wire the plugin","level":2,"anchor":"Step-4-Wire-the-plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construct and register "},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inside your "},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" factory:"}]},{"code":["import SwiduxPaywall","","let paywallPlugin = PaywallPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.paywall,","    action: AppAction.paywall,","    extractAction: { if case .paywall(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","    service: RevenueCatPaywallService()",")","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Step 5: Observe customer info on launch","level":2,"anchor":"Step-5-Observe-customer-info-on-launch"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Start the long-lived entitlement stream once, on the root view:"}]},{"code":["struct ContentView: View {","    @Environment(AppStore.self) private var store","","    var body: some View {","        RootContent()","            .task { store.send(.paywall(.observeCustomerInfo)) }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"observeCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns an effect that lives for the duration of "},{"code":"PaywallService.customerInfoStream()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Every snapshot the service yields flows through "},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and updates "},{"code":"store.paywall.isPro","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"hasPermanentLicense","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Step 6: Present the paywall","anchor":"Step-6-Present-the-paywall","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bind a sheet to "},{"code":"store.paywall.isPresented","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and dispatch ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".paywall(.dismiss)"},{"type":"text","text":" when it closes:"}]},{"code":[".sheet(isPresented: Binding(","    get: { store.paywall.isPresented },","    set: { if !$0 { store.send(.paywall(.dismiss)) } }",")) {","    PaywallSheet()","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Trigger presentation by dispatching "},{"code":".paywall(.request(reason:))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a short identifier describing why you’re asking. The reason is stored in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.requestedReason"},{"text":" so the sheet can tailor its copy.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["store.send(.paywall(.request(reason: \"export-pdf\")))"]},{"text":"Step 7: Gate a feature","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-7-Gate-a-feature","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read "},{"code":"PaywallState.isGateSatisfied","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" before running gated work. If it’s "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", dispatch "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".request"},{"type":"text","text":" instead:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["Button(\"Export PDF\") {","    if store.paywall.isGateSatisfied {","        store.send(.export(.exportPDF))","    } else {","        store.send(.paywall(.request(reason: \"export-pdf\")))","    }","}"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Step 8: Restore purchases","level":2,"anchor":"Step-8-Restore-purchases"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a restore button to your paywall sheet. Reflect ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.isLoading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to disable it while the call is in flight:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["Button(\"Restore Purchases\") {","    store.send(.paywall(.restorePurchases))","}",".disabled(store.paywall.isLoading)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On success, the resulting snapshot flows through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":" and updates the gate. On failure, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.error"},{"type":"text","text":" is set."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Step 9: Manage subscriptions","level":2,"anchor":"Step-9-Manage-subscriptions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For an existing subscriber, surface a button that deep-links into the system subscription management page:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["Button(\"Manage Subscription\") {","    store.send(.paywall(.openManageSubscriptions))","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This opens "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"itms-apps:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions"},{"type":"text","text":" via the plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"openURL"},{"type":"text","text":" handler, which routes to the App Store on iOS and Settings on macOS."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Testing","level":2,"anchor":"Testing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"MockPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to drive previews and tests into a known entitlement state:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["#Preview(\"Pro\") {","    let store = AppStore.configured(","        paywallService: MockPaywallService(isPro: true)","    )","    return ContentView().environment(store)","}","","#Preview(\"Free\") {","    let store = AppStore.configured(","        paywallService: MockPaywallService()","    )","    return ContentView().environment(store)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plumb the service through a parameter on your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"type":"text","text":" factory so previews can override it without touching the live RevenueCat SDK."}]}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"title":"How-to Guides","anchor":"How-to-Guides"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Add a Paywall","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"type":"topic","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},"https://github.com/heirloomlogic/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall":{"title":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","title":"Add a Version Killswitch"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"title":"Plugin Architecture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install the bundled "},{"code":"swidux-ref","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","title":"Getting Started with Swidux","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","abstract":[{"text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"title":"Add a Parental Gate","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","type":"topic"}}}